         <component>
            <section ID="id_link_4f86fe97-83a2-d94c-e063-6294a90a7a15">
               <id root="4f86fe97-83a1-d94c-e063-6294a90a7a15"/>
               <code code="71744-7" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="HEALTH CARE PROVIDER LETTER SECTION"/>
               <text>
                  <paragraph>Purpose:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>This product is being distributed in response to a shortage of Sterile Water For Injection, USP product in the United States as per U.S. Food and Drug; FDA Drug Shortgae List.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Regulatory Status:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>This product has not been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration but is being made available under enforcement discretion during a drug shortage.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Product Descritpion:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>This product only have Water for Injection, USP.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Dosing and Administration:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>The route of administration is intravenous. Product is not for direct intravenous use unless rendered nearly Isotonic. It can be used as a drug diluent. Following suitable admixture of prescribed additive, the final product dose is usually dependent upon the age, weight and clinical condition of the patient.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Safety Information:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>Additives may be incompatible. Please confirm compatibility.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Storage and Handling:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>Store at 20 to 25C (68F to 77F) [See USP Controlled Room Temperature]. </paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Reporting Adverse Events:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>Report adverse events to wwww.fda.gov/medwatch or 1-800-FDA-1088.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>Contact Information:</paragraph>
                  <paragraph>For any question or concern, please contact 1-863-292-2211. Email: Info@AssureIV.com.</paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph/>
               </text>
               <effectiveTime value="20260416"/>
            </section>
